{"File":"c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google Antigravity/Projects/Typikon Coded/.agents/references/learnings.md","LineNumber":608,"LineContent":"2. **Fast-Path Resolution**: Added lazy loading in `EngineCore` (`engine/core.py`) and fast-paths in `get_liturgical_context` (`engine/calendar.py`), `resolve_rubrics` (`engine/rubrics.py`), and `resolve_liturgy_readings` (`engine/resolvers/liturgy.py`) that bypass runtime calculations if an almanac for the queried year is present."}
{"File":"c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google Antigravity/Projects/Typikon Coded/.agents/references/learnings.md","LineNumber":655,"LineContent":"   - **Fix**: Isolated lookahead logic in [calendar.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/engine/calendar.py) (`_apply_lookahead`) to only execute when `is_sunday_vigil` is set. Hard-capped praises to 8 in [matins.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/engine/resolvers/matins.py) and praises formatter."}
{"File":"c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google Antigravity/Projects/Typikon Coded/.agents/references/learnings.md","LineNumber":668,"LineContent":"   - Transferred all liturgical classification logic (the assignment of `triodion_book`, `menaion_book`, `menaion_class`, and `saint_categories` fields) from frontend Javascript (`cantor_dashboard/main.js`) to the Python backend (`engine/calendar.py`)."}
{"File":"c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google Antigravity/Projects/Typikon Coded/.agents/references/learnings.md","LineNumber":675,"LineContent":"   - Fixed a bug where simple saints falling on moveable feasts (e.g. Pascha, Ascension, Pentecost) overrode the feast's rank code. Added `39` (Ascension), `49` (Pentecost), and `60` (Eucharist) to the `movable_overrides` map in `_lookup_dolnytsky_calendar`."}
{"File":"c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google Antigravity/Projects/Typikon Coded/.agents/references/learnings.md","LineNumber":676,"LineContent":"   - Guarded fixed calendar lookup to prevent overwriting `dolnytsky_rank_code` if a movable override has already set it."}
{"File":"c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google Antigravity/Projects/Typikon Coded/.agents/references/learnings.md","LineNumber":690,"LineContent":"   - Mapped `john the baptist`, `john the forerunner`, and `forerunner` to `Prophet` on the backend (`engine/calendar.py`) and frontend (`cantor_dashboard/main.js`)."}
{"File":"c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google Antigravity/Projects/Typikon Coded/.agents/references/learnings.md","LineNumber":714,"LineContent":"   - Multiple separate commemorations sharing a single rank tag in the raw calendar source must never be merged into a single description in [calendar_dolnytsky.json](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/json_db/calendar_dolnytsky.json). Doing so creates \"super person\" saints (e.g., December 4 St. Barbara \u0026 St. John of Damascus) and causes logic failures."}
